<!-- page 10 -->

Transformative AI and the implications for Tax and Legal

The shape of the AI future in tax and law

The AI advances society grapples with today do not simply represent another wave of technology change. Rather, transformative AI promises to reshape our world—shifting the foundations of how economies are taxed, how law and justice are administered, how professional expertise is applied.

The transition underway will test the ability of humans and institutions to adapt as quickly as the technology itself advances. The stakes are not limited to efficiency or cost, but extend to the integrity, fairness, and resilience of systems on which modern economies depend.

“Those who master the material define the era.”
—Ivan Zhao, co-founder and CEO of Notion, “Steam, Steel, and Infinite Minds”

